Drew's tasks for the coming week ...

Program 1.  Program to generate a set of N random cities

	- defaults to real values (at least 5 decimal places) inside a
	  unit square
	- the number of cities is a command line argument
	- writes cities to standard output, 1 city coordinate pair to a line
	- initializes random number generator by
			- second command line argument if there is one
			- otherwise uses clock
	
	*** single file program


Program 2.  Plots a set of N cities on the screen

	- reads the cities from standard input

	- surrounded by enclosing unit square border

	- coordinates on screen of enclosing square given on command line
	
	*** the "plot" is in a separate file from the main


(Completing the two above programs would be a satisfactory performance 
for this week.  A strong performance would include the following ...)


Program 3 Demo of Knowledge of Virtual Pages

	- Done by visualizing insertion method

	- updated path done on a second page, and then "slammed in",
	  that the change to the screen in "instantaneous"

	  (This program should be making use of the "plot" software from
	  program 2.)


